law.text:
		The Commissioner shall cancel the commercial feed license and product registrations of any person who fails to comply with the chapter by:

Failing to file the tonnage report;


Falsifying information;


Making an inaccurate statement of tonnage distributed in Virginia during any reporting license year;


Making an inaccurate listing of medicated feed, small packaged commercial feed, or specialty pet feed for registration;


Failing to pay the license, registration, or inspection fee;


Failing to accurately report any of the information required to be submitted under this chapter;


Failing to keep records for a period of three years; or


Failing to allow inspection of records by the Commissioner, as required by subsection F of § 3.2-4805.
